  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Showkat Ahmad Joo vs Ut Of J&K Through Financial ... on 4 April, 2024 Author: Rahul Bharti Bench: Rahul Bharti High Court Of Jammu & Kashmir And Ladakh At Srinagar Reserved on : 02.04.2024. Pronounced on : 04.04.2024. Case:- WP(Crl) No. 265/2023 Showkat Ahmad Joo, Aged about 35 years, S/o Farooq Ahmad Joo, R/o Green Colony Wuyan Pampore, District Pulwama (Detenue) Through his father Farooq Ahmad Joo Aged about 57 years, S/o Abdul Aziz Joo R/o Green Colony Wuyan Pampore, District Pulwama ....Appellant(s)/Petitioner(s) Through: Mr. Syed Sajad Geelani, Advocate Vs 1 . Ut of J&K through Financial Commissioner, (Addl. Chief Secretary) Home Department, J&K Jammu/ Srinagar. 2. District Magistrate Pulwama, Kashmir ..... Respondent(s) Through: Mr. Zahid Qaiz Noor, Ga Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Rahul Bharti, Judge Judgment",
    "facts": "The dossier related the petitioner to be a person in contact with various separatists and other fringe elements under whose influence the petitioner had become a radical and fundamentalist, acting as a provider of all possible assistance like food, shelter, finance, transportation besides acting as a courier of classified information regarding statement of movement of police and security forces to the Lashker-e-Toiba (LeT) and The Resistance Front (TRF). The petitioner is alleged to have been apprehended on 02.05.2023 in terms of Section 107/151 of Cr. P.C. and came to be released by furnishing of bond before the Executive Magistrate Ist Class, Pampore. It is with this backdrop that third time, instead of resorting to Section 107/151 Cr. P.C., the preventive detention under the J&K Public Safety Act, 1978 came to be applied against the petitioner by the respondent No. 2-District Magistrate, Pulwama.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
